#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1080.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130075} :activity/id #uuid "58849859-2309-5910-bd3d-67823d7df3a7" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049003 :topic/id #uuid "d28d3589-1bfc-578d-a6de-3fced37e42ca" :topic/math-academy-id 1996} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130075 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130400 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to evaluate the double integral  \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} 2(x+y)\\,\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the finite region bounded by the lines $x=0, \\, y=1, \\, y=2, \\, y=3-x,$ and $y=x.$ How do we proceed?\n\nTo evaluate an integral like this, we carry out the following steps: \n\n**Step 1.** Sketch the region $D$. This allows us to determine the precise set-up of our integral. \n\nIn this example, we obtain the following:\n\n![](images/0a/0a90a4f377327f5293308f1e08ac6596f1c27b9bd47a614d6d7cb1c5dbfec33c.png)\n\n**Step 2.** Split (if necessary) the region $D$ into several type I or II regions.\n\nFrom the diagram above, we see that our region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions $D_1$ and $D_2,$ as follows.\n\n![](images/a9/a93e1a0a0a7f9c104cb5d380b2a7ff98d6712ef0d2d67b74130da5dcf1701443.png)\n\n \n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x  \\leq 1, \\quad 1 \\leq y \\leq 2\\big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nD_2= \\{(x,y)\\: : \\: 1 \\leq x \\leq 3/2,  \\quad  x \\leq y \\leq 3-x\\}\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** Set up and evaluate the integral using the additivity property of double integrals. We recall the following fact:\n\n*If $D$ is the union of two sub-regions, $D_1, D_2$, that don't overlap then,*\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A = \\iint\\limits_{D_1}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A + \\iint\\limits_{D_2}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A.\n$$\n\nSo, finally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}2(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}2(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}2(x+y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{3/2}{\\int }_{x}^{3-x}2(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "ce229625-0660-5682-9e5a-3850f8ce33e5" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4358 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "677b9db4-978c-5d9a-9a29-29a0b08eb60b" :step/math-academy-id 26555 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130077}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130076 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129192 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129011 :question/id #uuid "b4697448-d5f7-59ae-86a1-689ae00ebb73" :question/math-academy-id "e-7197"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129616} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129620} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268864} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268866} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323935} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351404} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351405} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351418} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351419} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487311} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487362}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region"} :step/id #uuid "2f89bd90-2162-53d4-845f-4123449e769b" :step/math-academy-id 26556} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130077 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129193 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129012 :question/id #uuid "9a106b26-c6fe-5e4b-ae43-9cc02ddb67c1" :question/math-academy-id "e-7198"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "264eb5c1-fb55-5ed2-bc46-5548555bc98c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049997}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129615} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129877} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268856} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268857} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351391} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351417} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388258} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388265} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475920} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475923}] :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type I Regions"} :step/id #uuid "54b73f74-716d-5e9c-b4e0-441e927a08a5" :step/math-academy-id 26557 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130078}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130078 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129194 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129013 :question/id #uuid "be10aba9-930e-54c3-814d-8d089757affc" :question/math-academy-id "e-7199"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050264}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129614} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129617} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268860} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268861} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351394} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351395} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388272} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394366} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475948} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475969} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487322} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487337}] :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions"} :step/id #uuid "91c2533d-2b41-5369-944b-c1f361a0d1ca" :step/math-academy-id 26558 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130076}}] :activity/title "Double Integrals Over Partitioned Regions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186129341}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487409} :activity/id #uuid "b3aac3c7-90b7-533d-bf27-3ce859ab6fa7" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049003 :topic/id #uuid "d28d3589-1bfc-578d-a6de-3fced37e42ca" :topic/math-academy-id 1996} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487409 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351405 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "306a6506-07dc-5b0c-8392-0268c083fa9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{78}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348878} {:answer/id #uuid "713f1706-9cb1-5ca6-a6d0-c5010467a966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{48}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349489} {:answer/id #uuid "b31a9c8d-a546-5cc5-8480-da64dad9d7dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350034} {:answer/id #uuid "e26e4fa2-211b-5423-80e7-522445eb265c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{106}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350438} {:answer/id #uuid "e818788b-e985-59b3-9afa-d1a2bbb5a35f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{84}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350476}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350034} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f9af1a0-4416-5f2e-9bcd-4b88ecf8616c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350927}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "401eab2e-5c7c-5b79-aa17-72b56d139abb" :question/math-academy-id "q-82229" :question/problem "![](images/eb/ebb0b09ffab6ffdff6a04104b09d6904302fdb7580262663b5e0c65bd3f95502.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is enclosed by the the curve $y=(x-1)^{2}$ and the lines $y=x+1$ and $y=3-x,$ as shown in the picture. Evaluate ${∬}_{D}2y\\,dA.$" :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/f2/f26c3e1bbbc268308db8d419bc799ad5349673e97c8828471997a5d36cb94d7d.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le x+1\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le 3-x\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2y\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}2y\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}2y\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{(x-1)^{2}}^{x+1}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(x-1)^{2}}^{3-x}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}{|}_{(x-1)^{2}}^{x+1}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}{|}_{(x-1)^{2}}^{3-x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[(x+1)^{2}-(x-1)^{4}]\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}[(3-x)^{2}-(x-1)^{4}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(x-1)^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{1}+{[-\\frac{(3-x)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(x-1)^{5}}{5}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =((\\frac{8}{3}-0)-(\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{5}))+((-\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{5})-(-\\frac{8}{3}-0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{15}+\\frac{32}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "091d4923-4cda-500f-b9f4-8ac1e9d91cd5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487411}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487411 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487337 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40c55d33-ba55-5d27-b6a9-d7ed118cb44a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{(5-y)/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{(5-y)/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486734} {:answer/id #uuid "428d0559-241a-513a-a644-e6effb0a6188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{(5-y)/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{(5-y)/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486737} {:answer/id #uuid "46af8adc-4cca-5af5-9d41-ebbaade7dc42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486746} {:answer/id #uuid "502aa9c7-72b5-553e-8bc0-c460780a945a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{(5-y)/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486766} {:answer/id #uuid "766c7449-a808-5a55-b964-67fc339d2720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{y/2}^{(5-y)/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486852}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486766} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8ba307e-a764-5862-ad57-ced793b39140" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5f7eccff-14bb-598f-9945-41d3d8682a45" :question/math-academy-id "q-82359" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y=2x,$ $y=5-3x$ and $x=0.$\nExpress ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=2x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{2} \\\\ y=5-3x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{5-y}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/80/805f6d6117e6c9028cb63f1ff8328bc625dc992a1f270abecdf898df31204613.png)\n\n  \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/b3/b394a5a80ab4fafdcc7e5457f37360d693ddb7c24e1f6ed208ada3b778b3623c.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{y}{2}\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le y\\le 5,\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{5-y}{3}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{(5-y)/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "11f534ed-c297-588d-85ea-334d9dacbc9e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487442}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487442 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487322 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5079fcbf-12d5-555e-ba06-e724191b097b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{5/2-y/2}^{-3y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{y}}^{5/2-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486769} {:answer/id #uuid "6642da2a-f097-5ecf-a91f-4715e2d141b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-3y}^{5/2-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{5/2-y/2}^{2\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486819} {:answer/id #uuid "775bba60-5b7e-592b-b72e-c346f06aaecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{5-2y}^{-y/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}/4}^{5-2y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486855} {:answer/id #uuid "8e07fc70-9e57-50c8-b4a8-adf6ab4790be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-3y}^{5/2-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{y}}^{5/2-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486903} {:answer/id #uuid "a4da1d26-e778-5253-844a-78992934a403" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-y/3}^{5-2y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}/4}^{5-2y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486967}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486903} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b421256-f0c1-5cc3-b2b7-d51597f776a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "44184e7a-6e43-56fd-ad13-4a3507c85f19" :question/math-academy-id "q-132389" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4},$ and the lines $y=5-2x$ and $y=-\\frac{x}{3}.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & \\,⟹\\,x=2\\sqrt{y} \\\\ y=5-2x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{y}{2} \\\\ y=-\\frac{x}{3} & \\,⟹\\,x=-3y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/b0/b0f6f95d81c665d189d1b1e97f78b82b6c64abd5c1ae17ffe4f918e7650a7bcc.png)\n\n  \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/87/873c2a14782c1ceb96fc3c1c71888dd221761d21749824e39157671979a62f0f.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,-3y\\le x\\le \\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{y}{2}\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,2\\sqrt{y}\\le x\\le \\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{y}{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-3y}^{5/2-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{y}}^{5/2-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d2cd8827-9ddb-5ec8-81f6-c7a484c99c30" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487445}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487444 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487362 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "301acdf2-3133-5c96-9ed6-70f8f44f4187" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486694} {:answer/id #uuid "397659b0-ec2c-5443-99d4-e9399dc15f28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486716} {:answer/id #uuid "51946454-9503-53ce-8e7e-10961abf504f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486773} {:answer/id #uuid "7bc856e3-9183-589b-9c39-0b6070d8a463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486861} {:answer/id #uuid "f41919a2-22c7-507e-aeb5-2b2bdc28371e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487115}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486716} :answer-field/id #uuid "829bbe55-b655-5278-9ed1-de2eacfe24fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487212}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a42208da-aa4c-5f1b-858e-ec1e99355b8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-132427" :question/problem "![](images/01/019f0f9f83ddf323d543d109677335cb3ae72a200baf834453a0eca16a9353ba.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∬}_{D}6y\\,dA,$ where $D$ is the region shown in the picture above." :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/d2/d222e86f6af7c3ed2b35711114c9062d6f0c9b0f2551aa44cac33318c6e5813f.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,x+2\\le y\\le \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2\\le y\\le x+2\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}6y\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}6y\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}6y\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}6y\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}6y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}3{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}3[{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2)}^{2}-{(x+2)}^{2}]\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}3[{(x+2)}^{2}-{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2)}^{2}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}3(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+{x}^{2}-4x)\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}3(-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-{x}^{2}+4x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{20}+{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}){|}_{-2}^{0}+(-\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{20}-{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}){|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{3(-2)^{5}}{20}+(-2)^{3}-6(-2)^{2})-\\frac{3(2)^{5}}{20}-(2)^{3}+6(2)^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{5}+8+24-\\frac{24}{5}-8+24 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d94ab042-5d46-5024-9756-3d7da363c7dd"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487445 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487311 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "029b012c-3003-5a01-95de-49b3208f6126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486598} {:answer/id #uuid "2e141aa6-7892-5e90-8251-ada8c35b476a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486683} {:answer/id #uuid "412cf9ab-4bdc-5b78-83cf-8ae867c5f157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486735} {:answer/id #uuid "60afe4df-9c09-5b15-bbcb-fc0199d11762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486806} {:answer/id #uuid "d668b9c6-7114-590f-825d-f131aae6d230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487064}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487064} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d459e4e-8f77-5b7a-9a74-352c81c90d32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "307a3f33-b63b-5a72-91e6-852f4ed601a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-132425" :question/problem "![](images/79/797cddb4ea3cb41959df88e56517e9ee71e76e3cd08a9a93d2957b9792d14abb.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∬}_{D}12x\\,dA,$ where $D$ is the region shown in the picture above." :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/0e/0e69b1cb480b87216273db4336adff57cbf9d9bc450aac4b0cdb58b1ae63f6f7.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-3\\le x\\le 0,\\,-\\frac{2x}{3}\\le y\\le \\frac{x}{3}+3\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\frac{4x}{3}\\le y\\le \\frac{x}{3}+3\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}12x\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}12x\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}12x\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{-2x/3}^{x/3+3}12x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{4x/3}^{x/3+3}12x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}12xy\\,{|}_{-2x/3}^{x/3+3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}12xy\\,{|}_{4x/3}^{x/3+3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}12x[\\frac{x}{3}+3+\\frac{2x}{3}]\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}12x[\\frac{x}{3}+3-\\frac{4x}{3}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}12x(x+3)\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}12x(3-x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}(12{x}^{2}+36x)\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}(36x-12{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(4{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}){|}_{-3}^{0}+(18{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3}){|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =-(4(-3)^{3}+18(-3)^{2})+18(3)^{2}-4(3)^{3} \\\\  & =108-162+162-108 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "dc59d81a-3089-5b64-95b6-f5767562fa8e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487444}}] :activity/title "Double Integrals Over Partitioned Regions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486592}]}
